+//   K: the five transposed dword reads of a key row (dwords 0, 8, 16, 24, 26 of the head),
+//      the scales' places, the two splices of the blocks that start 2 bytes off a dword,
+//      the eight 4-dword sets, B16 (the codes as f16 1152 + code by integer operations),
+//      Q's lane order (KV8_ORD), the accumulator's start (-1152 sum q) and the scale a block;
+//   V: the transformed byte reads (lane = byte column, 32 key rows) at V8X's columns, the
+//      third read and lane splice of a block that starts 2 bytes off a dword, the output's
+//      dim map (KV8_ODIM), the scales gathered a key in B16's key order, pe = f16(f16(p) d
+//      128), the start -1152 sum pe, and the 1/128.
+// Every modelled 2D read is also held to cl_intel_subgroup_2d_block_io's stated limits
+// ("behavior is undefined unless"): a base on 64 bytes, the first coordinate a multiple of
+// 4 for 8-bit data (of 2 for 16-bit), a width of 64 to 2^24 bytes and a multiple of 4 for
+// 8- and 16-bit data (of the element size otherwise), a height of 1 to 2^24 rows, a pitch not
+// below the width and a multiple of 16.
+// What it does not: the DPAS and the block reads themselves (modelled as what the kernel
+// assumes of them: lane = row for the transposed read, lane = column and the rows in byte
+// order for the transformed one - the card run is what proves that), the online softmax
+// (a direct one here; port_kernel_model.py has the kernel's), register allocation.
+// Every modelled read is checked against the surface it names and against the tensor's own
+// bytes, so a read that leaves the head's 136 bytes or the buffer fails the test.
+// Three results a case, on a sample of tiles:
+//   model vs exact   the transcription against a double-precision attention on ggml's own
+//                    dequantized K/V and the f32 Q: must be below 1e-6 (the f16 rounding of
+//                    Q and P is all that separates them);
+//   CPU vs exact     the CPU backend's op, which quantizes Q to q8_0 for its dot product:
+//                    what a correct kernel's NMSE against the CPU reference will be about;
+//   model vs CPU     must be inside the bound the q8_0 port cases run at (1e-5).
+// Red: GGML_TEST_FA_PORT_KV8_RED=1 K's scale applied twice, =2 V's scale from the next
+// block, =3 the two splices left out (a block that starts 2 bytes off a dword read as if
+// it started on one), =4 Q in dim order instead of KV8_ORD. Each must FAIL every case.
+// =5 is the V read as first written - at the code's own byte column, 2 mod 4 for blocks 0
+// and 2: the same numbers (the model reads any byte), and half of the V reads off the grid
+// the extension defines. It must FAIL on the rule count alone.
